X,

I received X-CEED Tech Solutions LLC=E2=80=99s purported =E2=80=9Cfinal rej=
ection.=E2=80=9D It is
rejected in full.

Your letter does not close this matter. It confirms that X-CEED is
attempting to avoid payment after work was requested, accepted, benefited
from, and then acknowledged in writing.

Your position is legally and factually defective.

First, X-CEED=E2=80=99s unsigned-agreement argument is not the end of the a=
nalysis.
Under Michigan law, the absence of a fully executed final writing does not
automatically defeat an agreement or payment obligation where the parties=
=E2=80=99
conduct, communications, role representations, accepted services, and
payment admissions show an agreement or benefit received. Whether a party
intended to be bound only by a later formal document is a factual issue,
not something X-CEED can unilaterally decide after receiving the benefit of
work.

Second, your reliance on an isolated clause from the same draft you claim
has =E2=80=9Cno legal authority=E2=80=9D is internally inconsistent. X-CEED=
 cannot treat
the draft as void for compensation purposes while selectively invoking
language from that same draft when convenient. In any event, the clause you
quoted concerns waiver. It does not erase Discord messages as evidence of
authorization, role representation, payment discussions, work performed,
admissions, or benefit received.

Third, if X-CEED=E2=80=99s position is that no signed employment agreement =
existed,
then the claim proceeds under alternative theories, including payment for
requested services, accepted services, quantum meruit, unjust enrichment,
and any applicable wage or compensation remedies. Michigan law does not
allow a party to request and accept valuable services and then retain the
benefit while paying nothing merely by saying the final employment document
was unsigned.

Fourth, your double-billing accusation is unsupported. If X-CEED claims
fraud or double-billing, identify the exact date, exact time block, exact
service, exact amount, exact false statement, evidence relied upon, and
legal basis. Broad accusations are not evidence. Accusation language does
not substitute for an itemized dispute.

Fifth, the record contradicts X-CEED=E2=80=99s current position. The preser=
ved
Discord record and local archive show that work was performed, X-CEED
represented my role, payment was discussed, and you confirmed in writing
that I would be paid for the work I did. After that admission, you shifted
positions repeatedly: reduction due to =E2=80=9Crecent events,=E2=80=9D pay=
ment withheld
pending investigation, =E2=80=9Csuspect until deemed innocent,=E2=80=9D no =
payment unless a
notarized statement was provided, and now an unsigned-contract denial.

That is not a coherent payment defense. That is a changing explanation
after X-CEED received the benefit of work.

Sixth, the notarized-statement demand is separately preserved. You
attempted to condition payment or compliance on my signing a notarized
admission against myself while fraud accusations and payment withholding
were already being used against me. I will not sign or notarize any
admission as a condition of payment. That evidence is preserved for
submission to the appropriate authorities for review.

The amount due remains $1,954.90 for X-CEED work performed from May 19,
2026 through removal/termination on May 29, 2026 at approximately 2:55 AM,
calculated from the agreed weekly pay amount of $1,352.00 per week.

Demand is again made for payment of $1,954.90 within 48 hours.

If X-CEED disputes any portion of this amount, provide a legally sufficient
itemized dispute within the same 48-hour period identifying:

   1.

   the exact dates disputed;
   2.

   the exact time blocks disputed;
   3.

   the exact work or services disputed;
   4.

   the exact amount disputed;
   5.

   the evidence relied upon;
   6.

   the legal or contractual basis for withholding payment.

A general accusation of fraud, an unsigned-contract argument, a separate
Xerox/XBUniverse dispute, a =E2=80=9Ctrust=E2=80=9D issue, or an internal i=
nvestigation is
not an itemized payment dispute.

X-CEED is directed to preserve all evidence relating to this matter,
including Discord messages, internal discussions, screenshots, files,
drafts, role assignments, payment discussions, local records, project
records, business records, and any communications involving
Xerox/XBUniverse. Do not delete, alter, conceal, or destroy evidence.

If payment is not made, and if X-CEED refuses to provide a specific lawful
basis for withholding payment, I will proceed through formal channels
without further informal debate. This includes wage/payment remedies, civil
recovery, claims for unpaid services, unjust enrichment, quantum meruit,
and submission of the fraud-accusation, payment-withholding, and
notarized-admission evidence to the proper authorities for review.

Nothing in this email is a waiver, release, admission, settlement offer, or
limitation of my rights. All rights, claims, remedies, compensation rights,
evidentiary rights, and reporting rights are expressly reserved.

